  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Research-Based Perspectives on the Psychophysiology of Yoga has generated a modest but meaningful scholarly footprint since its 2018 publication. OpenAlex records 12 citations, with uptake spread across articles, book chapters, and a review that engage yoga through mindfulness, autonomic regulation, and related health themes. The book also shows signs of pedagogical use through library holdings and a publisher-linked YouTube record, while its subject matter aligns with Gender equality as one documented SDG connection.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This book is positioned as a research-oriented reference on the physiological effects of yoga, and the citation record suggests that it has been used as a conceptual source for later work on yoga, psychophysiology, and mind-body interventions. The strongest signal is scholarly uptake: 12 OpenAlex citations place the book in a visible position within its field, with citation activity continuing from 2020 through 2026. That pattern points to steady, if concentrated, interest rather than a brief burst of attention.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing literature shows that the book\u2019s influence is extending into applied and interdisciplinary discussions of yoga and health. Later works cite it in contexts including mindfulness and compassion interventions, heart rate variability and autonomic control, complementary and alternative medicine, and mental health-oriented yoga programmes. The venues range from psychology and public health journals to integrative medicine and health studies, indicating that the book is being drawn into both clinical and conceptual conversations about yoga\u2019s effects.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Teaching and reference use are also visible in the record. WorldCat and OpenAlex holdings indicate library discovery, and the work appears in a publisher-hosted YouTube item with the title linked in the metadata, suggesting that it has been surfaced in a format compatible with instructional or promotional use. These signals do not prove classroom adoption on their own, but they do support a reading of the book as a pedagogical anchor for readers seeking an evidence-based introduction to yoga psychophysiology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The broader impact profile is comparatively quiet outside scholarly and library channels: there is no event archive available in the record, and downloads are not reported. Even so, the available evidence shows a book that has been taken up across a diverse citation landscape, especially in India but also internationally, and whose themes connect to ongoing work on health, psychology, and gender-related wellbeing. Overall, the book\u2019s record is best described as focused scholarly influence with some signs of teaching relevance, rather than wide public or event-based visibility.</p>",
